# SidCode: a Tools menu in the top level menu bar.
#
# The menu bar is assembled in two places, and a menu with nothing in it is dropped in two more,
# so a new top level menu has to be added to both builders and kept out of both drops or it never
# appears at all:
#
#   * What the renderer knows. MenubarToolsMenu is the menu id, kept beside the other menubar
#     ids. It is registered on MenubarMainMenu between Terminal and Help, in `order` - those
#     registrations are what the in-window menu bar is assembled from - and the id is
#     published to extensions as `menuBar/tools`, so that an extension can put its own items
#     inside it. That is what the SFTP extension's SFTP/FTP > Create uses.
#
#   * What the main process draws. On Linux and Windows, and on macOS - where the menu bar is
#     the application menu - the bar itself is assembled by Electron in
#     platform/menubar/electron-main/menubar.ts, and that file names every menu one at a time:
#     File, Edit, Selection, View, Go, Run, Terminal, Window (macOS) and Help. The *items* of
#     those menus arrive from the renderer as data, but which menus exist is decided there. A
#     menu the renderer registers and the main process does not name is silently never drawn:
#     the bar comes up as the eight it knows, whatever was registered. So Tools is named there
#     too, before Help.
#
#   * One line in the platform menu service, where an empty submenu is dropped from the list
#     the bar is built from. Tools is empty until an extension puts something in it, and the bar
#     is built while that is still true - so there is no Tools in the list, and a menu that is not
#     in the list is not on the bar. It cannot arrive later either: the Tools submenu's own change
#     event can fill in a menu the bar already has, but it cannot add one it does not have. Kept,
#     Tools comes up empty and the extension's items are in it a moment later. This is the change
#     that ends the hide-the-menu-bar-and-show-it-again ritual.
#
#   * One line in the renderer's own native menu bar builder: a menu that nothing has been
#     contributed to yet is skipped rather than treated as a broken menu bar. The whole bar is
#     sent as a single piece of data, so counting an empty Tools as an error would leave File,
#     Edit and the rest unsent along with it.
#
# A rebuild is needed for this one: it is the editor's own code, not a setting.
#

diff --git a/src/vs/platform/actions/common/actions.ts b/src/vs/platform/actions/common/actions.ts
--- a/src/vs/platform/actions/common/actions.ts
+++ b/src/vs/platform/actions/common/actions.ts
